{"id":"9cbfc4e655546c2cb8536c1214187b0b0d8f7a5b","axis":"silent","repo":"kestra-io/kestra","sha":"9cbfc4e655546c2cb8536c1214187b0b0d8f7a5b","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"ui/AGENTS.md","lines":["@@ -259,6 +259,8 @@ Rules:"," "," **A prop the component does not declare is a type error.** `vueCompilerOptions.checkUnknownProps` is on, with `data-*` and `aria-*` accepted everywhere. When vue-tsc rejects a prop, it is either dead (remove it) or forwarded through `$attrs` without a type (type it, as in \"When extending the design system\"). A library component missing a prop it forwards gets a typed re-export, like `DynamicScroller` below."," ","+**Keep `v-model`; fit the bound state to the child's model type.** When the model type rejects a binding (`undefined` from a cleared field, a wider union), widen the parent's ref (`ref<number | undefined>(0)`, read with `?? 0`) instead of splitting it into `:modelValue` + `@update:modelValue` with a conversion. Only a wrapper's binding to the Element Plus component it wraps stays split, since widening the wrapper's model would break every caller's `v-model` (`KsCheckbox`).","+"," **Import `DynamicScroller` from `src/utils/virtualScroller.ts`**, not from `vue-virtual-scroller`. `no-restricted-imports` rejects the direct import. Its 3.0.5 types (the latest) leave out what it forwards to `RecycleScroller` (`buffer`, `prerender`, `emitUpdate`, `updateInterval`, HTML attributes), and the re-export adds them."," "," **Never write `any`.** TypeScript stops checking a value the moment it is typed `any`, so a typo or a renamed field is found by whoever opens the page instead of by the compiler. The rule covers every spelling: `(row: any)`, `x as any`, `any[]`, `Record<string, any>`, in the `<script>` block and in template expressions alike."],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"ui/packages/design-system/src/components/Data/KsCollapse/KsCollapse.stories.ts","lines":["@@ -1,12 +1,12 @@"," import type {Meta, StoryObj} from \